OL,3,GNEWSAFencing call after horse killed on
OL,4,Aforest rail line
OL,5,
OL,6,FA horse owner and rider have called for
OL,7,Fbetter fencing alongside rail lines
OL,8,Fthrough the New Forest after their
OL,9,Fhorse was struck and killed by a train.
OL,11,FEight-year-old thoroughbred gelding
OL,12,FPerry bolted during an event on
OL,13,FSaturday and was able to get on to the
OL,14,Ftrack near Beaulieu Road station.
OL,16,FRider Amelia Anderson said it was a
OL,17,F"freak accident that should never have
OL,18,Fhappened".
OL,20,FNetwork Rail said it was "investigating
OL,21,Fthe circumstances".
